{"summary":"Restore correct hexadecimal digit conversion","explanation":"The regression changes the offset for alphabetic hex digits from 9 to 8. That maps A-F and a-f one lower than their hexadecimal values, causing the reported escape decoding failures. Restoring the offset fixes the conversion while preserving the existing CUnescape behavior.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/escaping.cc","old":"  if (x > '9') {
    x += 8;
  }","new":"  if (x > '9') {
    x += 9;
  }"}]}
